      "label": "Text",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Galactic Species Serial Number: Inorganic #27"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-8ff0ba9920d532cc"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Species Name: Tottonid"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-64b583ad70cc392e"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Galactic Nicknames: Electric Giant, Glowing Star Polyhedron, Respiring Boulder"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-de71681311c6b5c0"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Category: Kingdom Inorganic Organism - Class Silica - Order Monotectoid - Family Petragigas"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-a5bc2ba4d981b7b4"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Research Summary:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-09f67c944030cd12"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The home world of the Tottonids is a planet plagued by catastrophic storms."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "It was said that tornadoes that pass through will destroy everything in its path, leaving only the strongest and most resilient lives."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-f3910fcc64cf5164"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "This species appears as a translucent crystal with an internal logic center called a thought monotectic. Two individuals of this species would communicate with each other by emitting electric signals through this organ."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Their language, psyche, and history are unknown to the galaxy."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-ea08936008635142"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "In the era of the Mecha Wars, Tottonids were loyal sidekicks to the Mechas."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "After their defeat, the Tottonids were eradicated by organic creatures and became extinct."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Tottonids turn into mineral ores after their passing, and their past disease develop into splashes of colors within their bodies."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The Totton planet thus became a cavernous rocky planet blighted with storms."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-4cb5bae6be64f776"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "When the fires of war cleared, only a royal crown, which embodied the history of its monarchy, was left behind in the silent winds."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-00ff69c31934a047"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Related Curio:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-47ad00893912b9c8"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Unbearable Weight"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-1fb6228684283b83"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A Curio kept within the confines of the space station, appearing as a crystal-encrusted crown."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "It is actually the imperial crown from the silicon-based lifeforms of the Totton planet, a living fossil of the monarchy's history."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-2e1c4efce5d6dfc6"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "According to rumors, each deceased Tottonid emperor will have their logic center"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "embedded in this crown composed of the logic centers of previous emperors."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-823b2875b6c3a1b0"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The Tottonids believe this crown brings the wisdom of generations to its rulers."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "It's also the reason why the rulers of the Tottonid have always been unusually large, heavy, and beautiful."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-17fbe321848300e0"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "In the past few Amber Eras, there are scholars who believe that the crown actually stores racial memories and basic cells of the Tottonids."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "They also believe that exposing the crown to moonlight would allow them to touch the buried history of the race."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "With the kindling of life from that Aeon, this lost people of yesteryear can be given a rebirth."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-0e754480ef1a4144"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
